==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
It was recorded in the 17th century in England.<ref>[https://familysearch.org/search/record/results?count=20&query=%2Bgivenname%3Asamantha&birth_year0=1600]</ref>

Most probably a feminine form of {{m|en|Samuel}}, possibly influenced by {{m|en|Anthea}}. Other suggestions include {{m|arc|ܫܡܥܢܬܐ|tr=šemʿanta||[[listener]]|pos=noun}}, from {{m|arc|ܫܡܥ}}.

In India, Samantha can be interpreted as a variant spelling of {{m|en|Samanta}}, from {{der|en|sa|समन्त||[[universal]], [[adjacent]]}}.

